{"id":"n-20261011-o35j1f","category":"business","display_title":"Class-Action Lawsuit Against Banks","display_title_he":"תביעה ייצוגית נגד הבנקים","short_summary":"An Israeli court approved a major class-action lawsuit against four leading banks over uncompensated current account balances, sparking fierce debate among legal experts.","english_level":"C1","words":514,"reading_time":4,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Protestors_who_rallied_outside_Lafayette_Park_in_class-action_lawsuit_against_USDA_in_1997.jpg/960px-Protestors_who_rallied_outside_Lafayette_Park_in_class-action_lawsuit_against_USDA_in_1997.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"United States Department of Agriculture · Public domain","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Protestors_who_rallied_outside_Lafayette_Park_in_class-action_lawsuit_against_USDA_in_1997.jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"Globes","domain":"globes.co.il","url":"https://www.globes.co.il/news/article.aspx?did=1001558919","title":"התביעה שמטלטלת את הבנקים ועשויה לפתוח עידן חדש במערכת","published_at":"2026-10-11T07:00:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-11T07:00:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-11T14:07:39.673Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["A recent decision by the Central District Court in Lod has sent shockwaves through the Israeli banking system by approving a class-action lawsuit against four of the country's five largest financial institutions: Bank Leumi, Discount Bank, Mizrahi Tefahot, and the First International Bank. The legal challenge targets the management of current accounts during the period from 2022 to 2025, when the business environment experienced sharp interest rate hikes. According to the plaintiffs, including Noam Brodsky, Natalie Sherban, Saar Brodsky, and Zvi Hoch, the financial institutions should have either credited customers with interest on their current account balances or explicitly informed them that their funds could generate returns through alternative deposits. Plaintiffs estimate the total damage between 3.62 billion and 5.06 billion shekels, reflecting approximately 400 billion shekels held across the four banks in non-interest-bearing deposits.","Presiding Judge Shmuel Bornstein based his approval primarily on the legal doctrine of unjust enrichment, noting that while banks use these customer funds to generate lending revenues, they provide no interest in return. The judge stated that the bank generates a return exceeding the rate it would produce if it paid a fair and reasonable rate to its customers, creating an enrichment that justifies court intervention. However, the court dismissed other allegations presented by the plaintiffs, including claims of deception, breach of fiduciary duty, and bad faith. Market participants note that Bank Leumi holds the largest share of these current account funds at roughly fifty percent, followed by Mizrahi Tefahot at twenty-four percent, International at fourteen percent, and Discount at twelve percent. Meanwhile, a separate lawsuit involving Bank Hapoalim is already proceeding toward evidentiary stages.","Legal experts and economists remain sharply divided regarding the implications and validity of the ruling. Supporters argue that the decision represents a courageous step toward addressing unfair profit margins amassed by financial institutions during recent economic shifts. Former antitrust commissioner Prof. David Gila even suggested that additional grounds could have been established, viewing the major banks as monopolies exercising significant market power. Conversely, prominent legal scholars and attorneys contend that the ruling introduces a radical and legally questionable judicial intervention. Critics point out that banking relationships are governed by established contracts and that financial mediation requires banks to utilize deposited capital while maintaining liquidity for account holders, rather than operating like a physical safe. Furthermore, market observers emphasize that the court's stance directly contradicts the position of the Supervisor of Banks, who supported the financial institutions during the proceedings.","Looking ahead, the affected institutions are expected to file applications for leave to appeal to the Supreme Court, with Bank Discount explicitly noting it is weighing this step carefully. Legal analysts suggest that if the Supreme Court upholds the district court ruling, it could pave the way for massive settlement agreements reaching billions of shekels. Alternatively, if the decision is overturned, the proceedings themselves may still pressure regulators and banks to introduce enhanced consumer benefits and foster stronger market competition. Industry representatives warn, however, that retroactive financial liabilities could ultimately alter the pricing of credit and banking services for the general public, as systematic costs are rarely absorbed without adjustments."],"facts":[{"fact":"The Central District Court in Lod approved a class-action lawsuit against four major Israeli banks: Leumi, Discount, Mizrahi Tefahot, and International.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The lawsuit alleges that banks failed to pay interest on current account balances or inform customers about earning interest via deposits during the 2022-2025 period of rising interest rates.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The total damage claimed by plaintiffs is estimated between 3.62 billion and 5.06 billion shekels, based on around 400 billion shekels in non-interest-bearing deposits.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Judge Shmuel Bornstein approved the lawsuit under the legal doctrine of unjust enrichment while rejecting other claims such as deception and breach of trust.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Legal experts and economists are divided, with some praising it as a bold move against high bank profits and others criticizing it as a radical and legally flawed judicial intervention that contradicts the Banking Supervisor.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"recent","lemma":"recent","pos":"adj","he":"אחרון","name":false},{"text":"decision","lemma":"decision","pos":"noun","he":"החלטה","name":false},{"text":"Central District Court","lemma":"Central District Court","pos":"noun","he":"בית המשפט המחוזי מרכז","name":"true"},{"text":"Lod","lemma":"Lod","pos":"noun","he":"לוד","name":"true"},{"text":"sent shockwaves","lemma":"send shockwaves","pos":"verb","he":"הטיל טלטלה / עורר הדים","name":false},{"text":"Israeli","lemma":"Israeli","pos":"adj","he":"ישראלי","name":"true"},{"text":"banking system","lemma":"banking system","pos":"noun","he":"מערכת בנקאית","name":false},{"text":"approving","lemma":"approve","pos":"verb","he":"לאשר","name":false},{"text":"class-action lawsuit","lemma":"class-action lawsuit","pos":"noun","he":"תביעה ייצוגית","name":false},{"text":"four","lemma":"four","pos":"num","he":"ארבעה","name":false},{"text":"country","lemma":"country","pos":"noun","he":"מדינה","name":false},{"text":"five","lemma":"five","pos":"num","he":"חמישה","name":false},{"text":"largest","lemma":"large","pos":"adj","he":"הגדולים ביותר","name":false},{"text":"financial institutions","lemma":"financial institution","pos":"noun","he":"מוסדות פיננסיים","name":false},{"text":"Bank Leumi","lemma":"Bank Leumi","pos":"noun","he":"בנק לאומי","name":"true"},{"text":"Discount Bank","lemma":"Discount Bank","pos":"noun","he":"בנק דיסקונט","name":"true"},{"text":"Mizrahi Tefahot","lemma":"Mizrahi Tefahot","pos":"noun","he":"מזרחי טפחות","name":"true"},{"text":"First International Bank","lemma":"First International Bank","pos":"noun","he":"הבנק הבינלאומי","name":"true"},{"text":"legal challenge","lemma":"legal challenge","pos":"noun","he":"אתגר משפטי","name":false},{"text":"targets","lemma":"target","pos":"verb","he":"מתמקד ב- / נוגע ב-","name":false},{"text":"management","lemma":"management","pos":"nou